-- run: a `let` binding nothing reads is kept by `--release` when its
-- right-hand side may have an effect (`language.md` §6, *What an optimiser
-- may assume*; `backend.md` §9 item 1, as amended 2026-09-30).
--
-- `unread` is never read, and neither is `inList`, whose spawn sits inside a
-- list literal rather than at the top of the right-hand side. The fibers
-- they start are the point of writing them: each child prints a line, and
-- the parent sleeps so that both run before the scope ends. Until
-- 2026-09-30 the release optimiser dropped a named unread binding whole,
-- initialiser and all, so the release build started neither child and
-- printed only the last line, while the development build printed all
-- three. Both builds must print the same three lines.
import Io
import Node exposing (Program)
import Say
import Task


main : Program
main =
    Io.run
        (λ() ->
            ended =
                Task.scope
                    (λs ->
                        unread = Task.spawnIn s (λ() -> Say.say "spawned child ran")
                        inList = [ Task.spawnIn s (λ() -> Say.say "child in a list ran") ]
                        _ = Io.sleep 1
                        "scope ended"
                    )
            Node.print ended
        )
